\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\par
LICENSE SETUP\ulnone\fs24\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1\b0 Go to client area and select "Edit" at your license.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}\b0 Put the machine ip address at "Ip Address" field.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}\b0 Go to "MuServer\\Tools" folder and run "GetHardwareId.exe".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}\b0 Open "HardwareId.txt" and copy and put it at "Hardware Id" field.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 5.\tab}\b0 Click "Save changes".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 6.\tab}\b0 Go to "MuServer\\ConnectServer" and open "ConnectServer.ini".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 7.\tab}\b0 Put the license number at "CustomerLicenseId".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 8.\tab}\b0 Go to "MuServer\\DataServer" and open "DataServer.ini".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 9.\tab}\b0 Put the license number at "CustomerLicenseId".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 10.\tab}\b0 Go to "MuServer\\JoinServer" and open "JoinServer.ini".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 11.\tab}\b0 Put the license number at "CustomerLicenseId".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 12.\tab}\b0 Go to "MuServer\\GameServer\\DATA" and open "GameServerInfo - Common.dat".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 13.\tab}\b0 Put the license number at "CustomerLicenseId".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 14.\tab}\b0 Go to "MuServer\\GameServerCS\\DATA" and open "GameServerInfo - Common.dat".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 15.\tab}\b0 Put the license number at "CustomerLicenseId".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 16.\tab}\b0 Go to "MuServer\\MHPServer" and open "MHPServer.ini".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 17.\tab}\b0 Put the license number at "CustomerLicenseId".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 18.\tab}\b0 Done, if you had any errors check FAQ section.\b\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul\fs28 IP ADDRESS SETUP\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "ConnectServer" and open "ServerList.dat".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}\b0 Put the machine ip address at "IpAddress" column.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}\b0 Go to "Data" and open "MapServerInfo.txt".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}\b0 Put the machine ip address at "IpAddress" column.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 5.\tab}\b0 The following ports should be opened at the Firewall: 44405, 55900, 55919,55999.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 6.\tab}\b0 Done, if you had any errors check FAQ section.\b\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul\fs28 DATABASE SETUP\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1\ulnone\b0\fs24 Open "SQL Server Management Studio.exe".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}\b0 Click "Connect".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}\b0 On the top left side, right click "Databases".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}\b0 Click "New database...".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 5.\tab}\b0 On "Database name:" field put "MuOnline".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 6.\tab}\b0 Click "OK".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 7.\tab}\b0 Go to "MuServer\\DB" and double click "MuOnline.reg" and click "Yes" or "OK" to all windows.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 8.\tab}\b0 Double click "MuOnline.sql" and wait for a "SQL Server Management Studio" window open.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 9.\tab}\b0 On the top left dropbox select "MuOnline'.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 10.\tab}\b0 Click at "Execute" button.\b\par
{\pntext\f0 11.\tab}\b0 Done, if you had any errors check FAQ section.\b\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\par
\ul\fs28 RUNNING THE SERVER\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\ConnectServer" and run "ConnectServer.exe".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\JoinServer" and run "JoinServer.exe".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\DataServer" and run "DataServer.exe".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\GameServer" and run "GameServer.exe".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 5.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\GameServerCS" and run "GameServer.exe".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 6.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\MHPServer" and run "MHPServer.exe".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 7.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Done, if you had any errors check FAQ section.\ul\b\fs28\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\par
CLIENT SETUP\par

\pard 
{\pntext\f0 1.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnf0\pnindent0\pnstart1\pndec{\pntxta.}}
\fi-360\li720\sa200\sl240\slmult1\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\Tools\\GetMainInfo" and open "GetClientInfo.ini".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 2.\tab}\b0 Put the customername at "CustomerName".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 3.\tab}\b0 Put the the machine ip address at "IpAddress".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 4.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\Tools\\GetMainInfo" and open "GetMainInfo.ini".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 5.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Put the customername at "CustomerName".\b\par
{\pntext\f0 6.\tab}\b0 Put the the machine ip address at "IpAddress".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 7.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\Tools\\GetMainInfo" and run "GetClientInfo.exe".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 8.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Go to "MuServer\\Tools\\GetMainInfo" and run "GetMainInfo.exe".\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 9.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Now the folder "Tools\\GetMainInfo\\Path" is your client patch, copy its contents to the full client.\ul\b\fs28\par
{\pntext\f0 10.\tab}\ulnone\b0\fs24 Done, if you had any errors check FAQ section.\ul\b\fs28\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\par
FAQ (Frequently Asked Questions)\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24 Q: The error message box "Could not authenticate the machine" appears.\par
A: Redo the "LICENSE SETUP" part of the guide with more attention.\par
\par
Q: The error message box "The file is codified in UTF-8 BOM and cannot be read. Change it to UTF-8 and try again" appears.\par
A: Restore the file mentioned in the message and edit it with NOTEPAD++, do not use Windows Notepad.\par
\par
Q: At "DataServer" or "JoinServer" the message "Could not connect to database" appears.\par
A: Redo the "DATABASE SETUP" part of the guide with more attention.\par
\par
Q: There's a way to open the server faster?\par
A: You can use the StartUp located at "StartUp".\par
\par
Q: My "main.exe" isn't opening.\par
A: Redo the "CLIENT SETUP" part of the guide with more attention.\f1\fs22\lang10\par
}
